x11872 write x11871 2
x11873 text "At 4000 functions an A0 edit costs 706 tokens against 143854 for TypeScript, which is 203.8x fewer than TypeScript. At 1 function A0 costs 2.42x TypeScript's tokens and 2.29x Rust's. Sonnet, cache-adjusted."
x11874 puts x11872 x11873
x11875 call close x11874 
x11876 call open x11875 2
x11877 write x11876 2
x11878 text "Cost here is every token a model reads and writes to make one edit: the instructions it is first given (the primer), the code it reads, and its reply. A model edits one function through a scoped view: the function, the signatures it depends on, and its callers. The view stays the same size as the program grows; a numbered whole file does not, so A0's advantage grows with program size and reverses on a one-function file, where the primer dominates."
x11879 puts x11877 x11878
x11880 call close x11879 
ret x11880
end

